---
/*
 * /privacy/ — Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Policy for the open-design.ai marketing site and the local-first product.
 */
import Layout from '../../_components/sub-page-layout.astro';

const updated = 'August 25, 2026';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy Policy — OpenDesign',
  url: new URL('/privacy/', Astro.site).toString(),
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'OpenDesign', url: Astro.site?.toString() },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — OpenDesign"
  description="How OpenDesign (Powerformer, Inc.) handles data on open-design.ai and in the local-first OpenDesign app."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1 class="legal-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Powerformer, Inc.</strong> (“OpenDesign”, “we”, “us”) handles information in connection with the website <a href="https://open-design.ai">open-design.ai</a> and the local-first OpenDesign application.</p>

    <h2>1. OpenDesign is local-first</h2>
    <p>The OpenDesign desktop application runs on your own machine. Your projects, prompts, designs, and the API keys you provide for local BYOK (“bring your own key”) workflows stay on your device and are sent directly to the model providers you configure. We do not proxy, collect, or store your local design content or local BYOK keys on our servers.</p>

    <h2>2. Information the website collects</h2>
    <p>When you visit open-design.ai we collect limited, standard analytics to understand traffic and improve the site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Usage analytics</strong> — pages viewed, referrer, approximate location (from IP), device and browser type, via privacy-respecting analytics providers.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies / local storage</strong> — used for analytics and to remember preferences such as your language. You can control cookies through your browser and our cookie notice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use website analytics to understand how the marketing site is used, improve pages, and measure campaigns. With your consent, we may use your email to send product updates and community news. You can opt out at any time by contacting us at <a href="mailto:privacy@open-design.ai">privacy@open-design.ai</a>.</p>

    <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The website may use third-party analytics, hosting, and security providers. Outbound links such as GitHub, Discord, and YouTube are governed by those services’ own privacy policies.</p>
    <p>When you use OpenDesign locally, your prompts and keys go directly to the model providers you configure; their policies govern that processing.</p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>OpenDesign uses cookies and local storage on the marketing site to remember language preferences and support analytics. Security checks such as Cloudflare Turnstile may process device, network, and interaction signals to distinguish normal users from automated access.</p>

    <h2>6. Data retention and security</h2>
    <p>Website analytics events are retained for a limited period consistent with our analytics providers. We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect data we do process. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.</p>

    <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete personal data we hold, and to object to or restrict certain processing. You can also disable cookies in your browser. To exercise any of these, contact us (below).</p>

    <h2>8. International processing</h2>
    <p>Website analytics and hosting may involve transfers outside your country or region. Where law requires separate consent, standard contracts, or other cross-border mechanisms, we follow those requirements.</p>

    <h2>9. Minors</h2>
    <p>The OpenDesign website and local application are not directed to children under 13 (or the age required by your jurisdiction), and we do not knowingly collect their personal information. If we learn that we collected a minor’s information improperly, we will delete or restrict it as required by law.</p>

    <h2>10. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the “Last updated” date above.</p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy-related inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@open-design.ai">privacy@open-design.ai</a>. For product and community questions, you can also reach us via the <a href="https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design">OpenDesign GitHub repository</a> or the community <a href="https://discord.gg/mHAjSMV6gz">Discord</a>.</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .legal {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 0 80px;
      color: var(--ink, #262626);
      font-family: var(--sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }
    .legal-h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-family: var(--serif, Georgia, serif);
      font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    .legal-meta {
      margin: 0 0 28px;
      color: var(--ink-mute, #666);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .legal h2 {
      margin: 32px 0 12px;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }
    .legal p,
    .legal li {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .legal ul {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }
    .legal a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
